Building this package
======================

    dpkg-buildpackage -b -uc -us

`debian/rules`'s `override_dh_auto_build` runs `composer install` (network
access required) for both `application/` and `app4/` during the build,
vendoring third-party PHP dependencies straight into the binary package.
That's a deliberate departure from strict Debian-archive practice (where
every build dependency must itself be a packaged, offline build-dependency)
because this package is not intended for upload to the official Debian
archive -- it is built and distributed as a GitHub Release artifact /
private apt repository entry for deploying this fork. If this package is
ever proposed for the official archive, `application/composer.json` and
`app4/composer.json`'s dependencies would need to be packaged individually
first.

No test suite runs during the build (`override_dh_auto_test` is a no-op):
this build environment has no PHP/Composer/MySQL to run one against (see
docs/AUDIT.md #6). CI (`.github/workflows/`) builds and boots the package
in an Ubuntu and a `debian:13` container as the real verification step.
